    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from feeling passionate, have you felt unusually energetic, euphoric, or invincible lately, to the point where you might not even need much sleep?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Well, um... I guess you could say I've had some stretches where I just feel really, really lit up. Like, almost unstoppable? It's actually a wonderful feeling, honestly. It's like every idea I have for a project is just brilliant and everything clicks. I do stay up a bit later working on things when I feel like that, but I just thought I was being productive. Is that okay? I mean, I hope that's a normal part of the creative process. \n\nBut, um... I suppose there is another side to it. Sometimes, when I'm feeling that energetic, if a collaborator or a client makes even just a small comment or a tiny critique... I can get a little defensive. Or, well, I might snap at them. It's embarrassing to admit, because I really try to be professional and kind to everyone. It just feels like my reaction is a lot bigger than the situation warrants. I'm really trying to work on that, though. I don't want you to think I'm a difficult person to work with.",
